The review has been written to `docs/reviews/pv-sizing/pvsize-04-flat-roof-gcr-table.md`.

**Summary of 7 findings:**

- **1 High**: GCR-tilt coupling inconsistency — tilt is capped at 25° regardless of latitude, but GCR decreases with latitude. Low tilt enables higher GCR, creating a contradiction at high latitudes.
- **3 Medium**: Step-function latitude bands create 14% capacity cliffs at boundaries; no differentiation between commercial (ballasted, shallow) and residential (penetrating, steep) flat-roof racking; east-west dual-tilt sawtooth configurations are entirely unmodeled.
- **3 Low**: HARES extends GCR beyond EnergyPlus/SAM's intended scope (GCR is for 1-axis tracking only in those models); `usable_fraction(Flat)=0.70 × GCR` interaction may double-count spacing losses; GCR is not adjusted for azimuth deviation from south on flat roofs.
